<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/06A1">Remark <span data-tag="06A1">7.1.7.17</span>.</a> Let $U: \operatorname{\mathcal{E}}\rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ be a cocartesian fibration of $\infty $-categories. In §<a data-tag="031Q" href="/tag/031Q">7.3.9</a>, we will see that questions about general $U$-colimit diagrams $\overline{q}: K^{\triangleright } \rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{E}}$ can often be reduced to the special case where $U \circ \overline{q}$ is a constant diagram in $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ (see Proposition <a data-tag="031R" href="/tag/031R">7.3.9.3</a>) which can then be studied using the criterion of Corollary <a data-tag="06A0" href="/tag/06A0">7.1.7.16</a>. </p>
</article>
